      notes: '### Start\nExtract all 14 files. Serve the prebuilt `built/index.html` immediately over any static HTTP server or run `npm install && npm run dev` to edit the React + TypeScript source. `CUSTOMISE.md` covers swapping the background video, editing the staggered headline words, updating the three stat counters and customising modal copy.\n\n### Fonts, palette and video\nGoogle Font `Readex Pro` (weights 300–700) on a pure `#000000` canvas with `#ffffff` text, `bg-neutral-900/90 backdrop-blur` pills and white opacity variants (`white/40`, `white/70`, `white/90`); zero purple or indigo. The fullscreen looping `<video>` (`object-cover`, `autoPlay`, `loop`, `muted`, `playsInline`) sits behind a bottom black gradient overlay (`h-48 bg-gradient-to-b from-transparent to-black`).\n\n### Interaction & layout\nAll text is strictly lowercase: three staggered `.hero-title` `<h1>` words (`letter-spacing: -0.04em`, `line-height: 0.95`, `text-[14vw] md:text-[13vw]`) placed at `protect` (`top-[18%]`), `your` (`top-[38%]`) and `data` (`top-[58%]`); three stat blocks (`+65k startups use`, `+1.5b gb data was protected`, `+300k downloads`) with desktop diagonal dividers (`rotate-[20deg]` / `rotate-[-20deg]`); clicking `platform`, `solutions`, `company`, `support` or `get started` opens a monochrome interactive dialog with `Escape` dismissal.\n\n### Scope\nSingle-viewport hero showcase with no live key-management or authentication backend. Read `LICENCE.txt` and `THIRD-PARTY-LICENSES.txt` before publishing.',
